    <string name="wizard_view">View</string>
    <string name="wizard_controls_view">“View” hides the instructions so you can look at the picture; OK or Back bring them back.</string>
    <string name="wizard_controls_touch_view">Touch: tap the screen to show the instructions again</string>
    <string name="wizard_ana_glasses_text">Choose the glasses type and the side of the colored filters, for example Red - Cyan with the red filter on the left. A filter passes light of its own color: the eye behind the red filter sees the picture coded in red. The picture shows a grid behind the screen, a square at screen level and a row of circles coming from behind the screen (left) to in front of it (right).</string>
    <string name="wizard_ana_rb_note">Red - Blue glasses show only a black and white picture. Check the filter color: blue is easy to confuse with cyan (Red - Cyan) or magenta (Green - Magenta), which support color filters.</string>
    <string name="wizard_ana_check_text">Look with both eyes. The circles should go from behind the screen (left) to in front of it (right), the square stays at screen level. If the depth is reversed, the filter sides are mixed up: swap them (◀ ▶ in adjust mode). “Save” adds the “Calibrated” filter for these glasses and makes it the default one.</string>
    <string name="wizard_vr_check_text">Press “View” and look through the headset: the circles should go from behind the screen (left) to in front of it (right), the square stays at screen level, nothing doubles. If something is wrong, go back to the previous steps. “Save” stores the calibration.</string>
    <string name="wizard_ana_ghost_title">Ghosting</string>
    <string name="wizard_ana_ghost_left_title">Left eye: “%1$s” filter</string>
    <string name="wizard_ana_ghost_right_title">Right eye: “%1$s” filter</string>
    <string name="wizard_ana_ghost_left_text">Close the right eye and look with the left one, through the “%1$s” filter. The letter L is clear, and in place of R there may be a shadow, darker or lighter than the gray background. Change the ghost suppression (◀ ▶): if the shadow is darker than the background, increase it; if lighter, decrease it. Find the value at which the letter R is least visible (ideally not visible at all).</string>
    <string name="wizard_ana_ghost_right_text">Close the left eye and look with the right one, through the “%1$s” filter. The letter R is clear, and in place of L there may be a shadow, darker or lighter than the gray background. Change the ghost suppression (◀ ▶): if the shadow is darker than the background, increase it; if lighter, decrease it. Find the value at which the letter L is least visible (ideally not visible at all).</string>
